       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in that profile explains a higher dose. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **The dose is a typo.** You may have meant 40 mg or 100 mg, or 200 mg at most. Tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **You mean to go above the maximum on purpose.** That would be an off-label dose. If so, please confirm it, and tell me if you'd like a note on the order with the rationale, such as specialist or psychiatry input. I'd also suggest a pharmacy review and a baseline ECG.\n3. **Titration.** Usual practice is to start at 25\u201350 mg daily and increase by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg/day. I can enter a starting dose if this is a new start.\n\nWhich one do you want?"
